n# = (128, 12, 207, 3)\n#\n# Feature channels:\n# Channel 0: Traffic speed/flow (normalized)\n# Channel 1: Event embedding (768-dim -> projected to hidden dim)\n# Channel 2: Temporal features (time-of-day, day-of-week)\n```\n\n### Output Specification\n\n```python\n# Output shape per batch sample:\n# (batch_size, output_length, num_nodes, 1)\n# = (128, 12, 207, 1)\n#\n# Contains: Predicted traffic speed for next 60 minutes\n```\n\n---\n\n## 5. Key Dependencies and Versions\n\n### Core Requirements\n```\ntorch >= 1.9.0\nnumpy\npandas\neasydict\n```\n\n### For Event Encoding\n```\ngoogle-genai\ngoogle-cloud-vertexai\n```\n\n### External Library\n```\nbasicts  # Spatial-temporal model library\n```\n\n### For Data Processing\n```\nscikit-learn\nscipy\n```\n\n---\n\n## 6. Event Encoding Details\n\n### Coordinate Reading Function\n\n```python\ndef read_coordinates_from_file(file_path):\n    """\n    Reads coordinate pairs from CSV file (graph_sensor_locations.txt format).\n    Assumes CSV format: index,sensor_id,latitude,longitude\n    """\n    coordinates = []\n    try:\n        with open(file_path, \'r\') as f:\n            is_header = True\n            for line in f:\n                if is_header:\n                    is_header = False\n                    continue\n                \n                line = line.strip()\n                if line:\n                    try:\n                        parts = line.split(\',\')\n                        if len(parts) >= 4:\n                            lat = float(parts[2].strip())\n                            lon = float(parts[3].strip())\n                            coordinates.append(f"({lat}° N, {lon}° W)")\n                    except ValueError:\n                        print(f"Warning: Skipping non-numeric coordinate line: {line}")\n        \n        if not coordinates:\n            print(f"ERROR: No valid coordinates found in file \'{file_path}\'")\n            return None\n        \n        return coordinates\n    \n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f"ERROR: Failed to read coordinate file \'{file_path}\': {e}")\n        return None\n```\n\n### Timestamp Processing\n\n```python\ndef read_time_from_file(file_path):\n    """\n    Reads timestamps from HDF5 traffic data file.\n    Converts to minute resolution for event querying.\n    """\n    df = pd.read_hdf(file_path)\n    return df.index.values.astype(\'datetime64[m]\')\n```\n\n---\n\n## 7. Model Integration Pattern\n\nThe D2STGNN model follows this pattern:\n\n```python\nfrom .arch import D2STGNN\n\n# Create model instance\nmodel = D2STGNN(**MODEL_PARAM)\n\n# Forward pass with multimodal input\n# input: (batch, seq_len, num_nodes, 3)\n#   - Channel 0: traffic data\n#   - Channel 1: event embeddings\n#   - Channel 2: temporal features\noutput = model(input_multimodal)\n\n# Loss computation\nloss = masked_mae(output, target_traffic, null_val)\n\n# Backward pass\nloss.backward()\n```\n\n---\n\n## 8. Configuration Management Pattern\n\n```python\nfrom easydict import EasyDict\n\n# Create hierarchical config\nCFG = EasyDict()\n\n# Dataset section\nCFG.DATASET = EasyDict()\nCFG.DATASET.NAME = \'METR-LA\'\nCFG.DATASET.TYPE = TimeSeriesForecastingDataset\nCFG.DATASET.PARAM = EasyDict({...})\n\n# Model section\nCFG.MODEL = EasyDict()\nCFG.MODEL.NAME = \'D2STGNN\'\nCFG.MODEL.ARCH = D2STGNN\nCFG.MODEL.PARAM = MODEL_PARAM\n\n# Training section\nCFG.TRAIN = EasyDict()\nCFG.TRAIN.NUM_EPOCHS = 100\nCFG.TRAIN.OPTIM = EasyDict()\nCFG.TRAIN.OPTIM.TYPE = "Adam"\nCFG.TRAIN.OPTIM.PARAM = {...}\n\n# Use config throughout training\nrunner = CFG.RUNNER(CFG)\nrunner.train()\n```\n\nThis hierarchical approach makes configuration management clean and extensible for LibCity integration.\n\nEOF\ncat /home/wangwenrui/private/shk/agentCity/repos/FUSE-Traffic/CODE_SNIPPETS.md\n', 'description': 'Create detailed code snippets and architecture document'}
