ENT ENCODING (gemini.py)\n\n**Purpose**: Transform unstructured event data into embeddings for traffic prediction\n\n**Architecture**:\n```\nSensor Coordinates + Timestamps\n         |\n         v\nGemini 2.5 Pro LLM (Location-aware event detection)\n         |\n         v\nEvent Descriptions (JSON)\n         |\n         v\nTextEmbeddingModel (text-embedding-005)\n         |\n         v\n768-D Embeddings (per sensor, per timestamp)\n```\n\n**Key Features**:\n- Identifies events 60-115 minutes ahead (predictive)\n- Geographic context via sensor coordinates\n- Event types: weather, concerts, crime, news\n- Output: 768-dimensional vectors (float32)\n- Storage: NPZ (compressed NumPy format)\n\n**Function Breakdown**:\n- `read_coordinates_from_file()`: Parse sensor locations from CSV\n- `read_time_from_file()`: Extract timestamps from HDF5 traffic data\n- `main()`: Orchestrate event generation and embedding\n\n**Dependencies**:\n```\ngoogle-genai (Gemini API)\nvertexai (Google Cloud)\npandas (data handling)\nnumpy (array operations)\ntqdm (progress tracking)\n```\n\n### 2. MODEL ARCHITECTURE (D2STGNN)\n\n**Type**: Dual-stream Temporal-Spatial Graph Neural Network\n\n**Input Modalities** (num_modalities=2):\n1. Traffic time series (1D per sensor)\n2. Event embeddings (768D, projected to hidden dim)\n\n**Spatial-Temporal Parameters**:\n```\nInput length:           12 time steps (60 minutes at 5-min resolution)\nOutput length:          12 time steps (60 minutes ahead)\nHidden dimension:       32\nTemporal kernels:       3\nSpatial kernels:        2\nNetwork depth:          5 layers\nDropout:                0.1\n```\n\n**Embedding Components**:\n- Node embeddings: 10-12 dimensions (learnable per-node features)\n- Time-of-day embeddings: 288 values (5-min resolution over 24h)\n- Day-of-week embeddings: 7 values (weekly periodicity)\n\n**Graph Construction**:\n- Adjacency matrices from road network topology\n- Transformation: "doubletransition" variant\n- Multiple adjacency matrix support for multi-scale spatial relations\n\n### 3. TRAINING CONFIGURATION\n\n**Dataset Variants**:\n\n| Parameter | METR-LA | PEMS-BAY | PEMS03 |\n|-----------|---------|----------|--------|\n| Nodes | 207 | 325 | 358 |\n| Batch Size | 128 | 64 | 128 |\n| Warm Epochs | 0 | 30 | 30 |\n| CL Epochs | 6 | 3 | 3 |\n| Node Hidden | 10 | 12 | 12 |\n\n**Optimization**:\n- Optimizer: Adam\n- Learning rate: 0.002\n- Weight decay: 1e-5\n- Gradient clipping: 5.0 max norm\n- LR scheduler: MultiStepLR with milestones\n\n**Training Strategy**:\n- Curriculum learning enabled\n- Warm-up phase to stabilize training\n- Progressive prediction length increase\n- Z-score normalization with rescaling\n\n**Evaluation Metrics**:\n- MAE (Mean Absolute Error) - Primary\n- MAPE (Mean Absolute Percentage Error)\n- RMSE (Root Mean Squared Error)\n\n---\n\n## Data Fusion Mechanism\n\n### Multi-Modal Input Integration\n\nThe model processes three parallel streams:\n\n```\nTraffic Stream              Event Stream              Temporal Stream\n(historical speeds)      (event embeddings)     (time indicators)\n       |                        |                        |\n       v                        v                        v\n[Traffic Encoder]        [Embedding Projection]  [Temporal Embedder]\n       |                        |                        |\n       +---------> [Multi-Modal Fusion Module] <--------+\n                              |\n                              v\n                    [Spatial-Temporal Blocks]\n                              |\n                              v\n                    [Traffic Prediction Head]\n```\n\n### Feature Composition\n\n**Input Tensor Shape**: (batch_size, seq_length, num_nodes, num_features)\n- Example: (128, 12, 207, 3)\n\n**Feature Channels**:\n- Channel 0: Normalized traffic speed\n- Channel 1: Event embedding (768D -> projected to hidden dim)\n- Channel 2: Combined temporal features (time-of-day + day-of-week)\n\n**Fusion Strategy**:\n- Early fusion at input level\n- Shared spatial-temporal processing\n- Target-specific output (traffic only)\n\n---\n\n## Data Requirements\n\n### Input Data Formats\n\n**Traffic Data (.h5)**\n- Format: HDF5 time series\n- Index: DateTime (5-minute intervals)\n- Content: Speed/flow per sensor\n- Datasets: METR-LA, PEMS-BAY, PEMS03\n\n**Sensor Coordinates (.txt)**\n- Format: CSV with header\n- Columns: index, sensor_id, latitude, longitude\n- Used for: Geographic context in LLM prompts\n\n**Adjacency Matrices (.pkl)**\n- Format: Python Pickle\n- Type: NumPy/sparse matrices\n- Variants: Multiple transformation types\n\n**Event Embeddings (.npz)**\n- Format: Compressed NumPy\n- Shape: (num_timestamps, num_sensors, 768)\n- Type: float32\n- Generated: By Gemini + TextEmbeddingModel\n\n### Output Specification\n\n**Predictions**:\n- Shape: (batch_size, output_length, num_nodes, 1)\n- Type: float32\n- Content: Predicted traffic speed for next 60 minutes\n\n---\n\n## Framework & Dependencies\n\n### PyTorch\n- Version: >= 1.9.0\n- Usage: Core deep learning framework\n- Distributed training: Supported via config\n\n### Google Cloud APIs\n- Gemini 2.5 Pro: Event detection\n- Vertex AI: Text embedding model\n- Credentials: Required GCP service account\n\n### Supporting Libraries\n```\nnumpy           # Array operations\npandas          # Data manipulation\neasydict        # Config management\ntqdm            # Progress bars\nscikit-learn    # Metrics and preprocessing\nscipy           # Scientific computing\nbasicts         # External ST model library\n```\n\n### Python Version\n- Minimum: 3.6\n- Recommended: 3.8+\n\n---\n\n## Training Workflow\n\n### Pre-processing Pipeline\n1. Load traffic data from HDF5\n2. Load sensor coordinates\n3. Query Gemini API for event descriptions\n4. Generate event embeddings via TextEmbeddingModel\n5. Normalize traffic data (Z-score)\n6. Create time-of-day and day-of-week embeddings\n7. Construct feature tensors\n\n### Training Loop\n```python\nfor epoch in range(num_epochs):\n    # Warm-up phase\n    if epoch < warm_epochs:\n        train_without_curriculum()\n    \n    # Curriculum learning phase\n    else:\n        gradually_increase_prediction_length()\n        train_with_curriculum()\n    \n    # Validation\n    validate()\n    \n    # Learning rate scheduling\n    update_learning_rate()\n    \n    # Save checkpoints\n    if improved:\n        save_checkpoint()\n```\n\n### Loss Function\n- **Primary**: Masked MAE (handles null values)\n- **Masking**: Applied to invalid traffic values\n- **Optimization**: Adam with weight decay\n\n---\n\n## Key Design Features\n\n### 1. Event-Aware Prediction\n- Future-oriented event detection (60-115 min ahead)\n- LLM-based semantic understanding of events\n- Geographic awareness via sensor coordinates\n\n### 2. Bimodal Architecture\n- Flexible multi-modality support (num_modalities=2)\n- Extensible for additional data sources\n- Unified spatial-temporal processing\n\n### 3. Temporal Awareness\n- Fine-grained time-of-day embeddings (288 values)\n- Weekly periodicity modeling\n- Curriculum learning for progressive forecasting\n\n### 4. Robust Training\n- Gradient clipping for stability\n- Learning rate scheduling with milestones\n- Masked metrics handling null values\n\n---\n\n## Challenges & Limitations\n\n### 1. Repository Status\n- Minimal code distribution (configs only)\n- D2STGNN architecture in external library (basicts)\n- Missing full implementation details\n\n### 2. External Dependencies\n- Requires Google Cloud Platform\n- Gemini API availability and cost\n- API response variability (non-deterministic)\n\n### 3. Data Constraints\n- Specific dataset format requirements\n- Pre-computed adjacency matrices needed\n- Sensor coordinate data essential\n\n### 4. Reproducibility\n- LLM-based event generation varies\n- No seed configuration visible\n- API responses non-deterministic\n\n---\n\n## Migration Path to LibCity\n\n### Phase 1: Model Integration\n```\n1. Clone basic